**REVISE — T219. Primary classification `UNBOUND-SCHEDULE`.**

| Dimension | Score | Evidence |
|---|---:|---|
| parameter-table-complete | 0.75 | §2.1 binds entry order, grid traversal, counts, and timing. Icon presence and tag position from §1.4 still lack keys or explicit derivations. |
| construction-priced | 0.90 | §§1.5, 2.1–2.2 price SVG, reject three alternatives, and bind sequencing and tile emphasis through phase validation and the frame/tag. |
| execute-checklist-ready | 0.90 | §2.4 specifies the cut, both HTML files, shared controls, handle offset, phone stacking, and self-check sequence. |
| verify-checklist-instrumented | 0.65 | §§2.3–2.4 name probes, swap values, grep patterns, inventory, and the prewave call point. Some probes do not test their stated property, and the fit instrument is deferred. |
| failure-points-priced | 0.85 | §2.5 prices phone fit, tile order, grid density, the icon split, and the render-proof limitation. |
| plateau-priced | 1.00 | §2.5 records FIRST ATTEMPT and names motion fidelity as the likely low lens, with a cause and a `scores.md` follow-through. |

**Named charges**

1. **`UNBOUND-SCHEDULE` — tile timing contradicts CP2.** Source 309.0 s maps to 4,000 ms. Under §2.1, Pennsylvania reaches full size at `1800 + 2200 = 4000 ms`, but §1.3 CP2 requires it to be full while Virginia is still growing. Those two conditions agree with the table. The mapping defect is that §2.3 skips CP2 and substitutes a both-complete probe at 4,500 ms. CP1’s probe also accepts any positive Pennsylvania scale, although the census says approximately 40%. Bind the easing and assert the CP1 scale and CP2 split state at their census instants. Add the missing CP10 hold receipt at 20,000 ms. [T219 record, §§1.3, 2.1, 2.3](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md)
2. **`UNBOUND-VARIABLE` — finish the parameter bindings.** Give icon presence and the tag’s corner offset explicit CONFIG keys or derivations. Define how `palette.frame` drives enslaved numeral color, since §2.1 also declares a separate `palette.enslavedNum` and §2.4 expects one palette edit to change both. [T219 record, §§1.4, 2.1, 2.4](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md)
3. **`CHECKLIST-INTENTION` — repair the swap and verification instruments.** Alpha inherits the tagged first slot, so the test cannot prove the tag moves. Swap the tagged slot and supply both `enterIdx` values. State whether the content and timing swaps run separately. With both edits applied, the last square completes at `16500 + 8 × 55 + 400 = 17340 ms`, so the 17,500 ms mid-fade probe would fail. Specify the actual SVG ink-measurement method, executable shared-control and duration checks, and the five named lens assignments. [T219 record, §§2.3–2.5](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md)

**Census and count disposition.** The offset is 305,000 ms. The default grids finish at 16,170 ms for Pennsylvania and 16,500 ms for Virginia, consistent with both fading at CP8 and complete at CP9. The count matches the table at 2 states and `21 + 15 = 36` squares. CP11–CP12 are covered by the named portrait deferral, and CP13 is the documented T220 boundary. [T219 record, §§1.3, 2.1, 2.3](runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T219-observe-plan.md)

**Limits.** This is a Plan judgment against the filed census. Source playback, rendered fit, and comparison behavior were not independently verified.

